1
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,903
April 27, 2019.

2
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:14,350
Houston, Texas.

3
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:16,190
A high school regional meet.

4
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:18,540
A senior from Strake Jesuit lines up in

5
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,010
the 100… and runs 9.98.

6
00:00:21,367 --> 00:00:22,160
9.98.

7
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:23,050
In high school.

8
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:43,950
Now the wind was way over the legal limit,

9
00:00:43,970 --> 00:00:45,700
so it don't count as a record.

10
00:00:45,990 --> 00:00:47,220
But it ain't matter.

11
00:00:47,530 --> 00:00:49,900
By the next morning that clip was everywhere.

12
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:54,640
ESPN, CBS, Fox, Sports Illustrated.

13
00:00:54,730 --> 00:00:56,570
Everybody callin' him "White Lightning."

14
00:00:56,590 --> 00:00:59,900
People sayin' he the next Usain Bolt.

15
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:02,450
His name was Matthew Boling.

16
00:01:02,470 --> 00:01:05,877
And 7 years later, ain't nobody talkin'

17
00:01:05,897 --> 00:01:07,310
'bout him like that.

18
00:01:07,330 --> 00:01:09,100
So what happened?

19
00:01:09,990 --> 00:01:12,963
Now first, let's get 1 thing straight.

20
00:01:12,983 --> 00:01:15,370
This kid was not a fluke.

21
00:01:15,650 --> 00:01:18,020
That same season, at the Texas state meet,

22
00:01:18,250 --> 00:01:19,550
he run 10.13.

23
00:01:19,570 --> 00:01:20,910
Legal wind.

24
00:01:20,930 --> 00:01:23,360
That's the US high school record.

25
00:01:23,810 --> 00:01:25,430
He won the long jump too.

26
00:01:25,450 --> 00:01:26,910
He was jumpin' 26 feet.

27
00:01:26,930 --> 00:01:36,745
And then he anchor the 4x400.

28
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:45,920
He get the stick over 20 meters behind…

29
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:50,820
and run a 44.74 split to win it.

30
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,290
In high school.

31
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:14,460
He won Gatorade National Athlete of the

32
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:15,330
Year.

33
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:18,490
And that summer at the Pan Am U20 Championships,

34
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:20,265
he took 4 gold medals.

35
00:02:20,285 --> 00:02:23,360
100, 200, and both relays, and both relays

36
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:24,990
set world U20 records.

37
00:02:25,290 --> 00:02:27,090
Oh, and the nickname?

38
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:29,310
He said he ain't even like it.

39
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:32,710
He didn't want his race being the story.

40
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:35,110
He just wanted to run.

41
00:02:40,690 --> 00:02:42,240
So he committed to Georgia.

42
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:45,340
And everybody figured this the start of

43
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:46,210
somethin' crazy.

44
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:09,740
His 1st year at Georgia, COVID shut the

45
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:11,337
whole season down.

46
00:03:11,513 --> 00:03:14,760
2021, he come back and win the NCAA indoor

47
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:23,357
title in the 200.

48
00:03:30,687 --> 00:03:31,537
20.19.

49
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:41,280
And for a minute, it look like the hype

50
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:42,710
was right on schedule.

51
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:44,830
Then the Olympic Trials.

52
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:48,743
He go out in the semis of the 100.

53
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:50,270
14th.

54
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,460
And in the 200?

55
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:51,820
9th.

56
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:52,540
1 spot.

57
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:54,370
1 spot from the final.

58
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:12,020
That was the 1st time it hit.

59
00:04:12,670 --> 00:04:14,300
This ain't high school no more.

60
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:18,190
And here go the part people forget.

61
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:21,940
2022, he run 9.98 again.

62
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:23,500
Except this time?

63
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:24,880
Legal wind.

64
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:28,560
And a couple weeks later he run 19.92 in

65
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:29,000
the 200.

66
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:46,099
He won the SEC in the 200, took 2nd at NCAAs.

67
00:04:47,210 --> 00:04:48,810
So he ain't slow.

68
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:52,530
He a sub-10, sub-20 sprinter.

69
00:04:52,550 --> 00:04:54,723
But at USAs?

70
00:04:54,743 --> 00:04:55,290
6th.

71
00:04:55,310 --> 00:04:58,950
And in America, 6th don't make the team.

72
00:04:58,970 --> 00:05:03,210
You can be top 10 in the world in the 200

73
00:05:03,230 --> 00:05:06,670
and still be stayin' home, 'cause the US

74
00:05:06,690 --> 00:05:08,200
is just that deep.

75
00:05:09,375 --> 00:05:10,225
2023.

76
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,820
He win the indoor NCAA title in the 200

77
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:14,690
again.

78
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:29,580
But outdoors, he don't even make the final.

79
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:31,710
So he try somethin' different.

80
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:33,200
The 400.

81
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:36,430
At USAs he finish 6th again.

82
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:38,920
But this time it got him on the relay pool

83
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:40,630
for Worlds in Budapest.

84
00:05:56,900 --> 00:06:00,070
And mane… he ran the 3rd leg of the mixed

85
00:06:00,170 --> 00:06:00,680
4x400.

86
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:02,140
Gold medal.

87
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:18,320
World record.

88
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:21,280
He ran the heat of the men's 4x400 too,

89
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:23,250
and they won that.

90
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:24,320
So on paper?

91
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:27,500
Matthew Boling a 2-time world champion.

92
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:30,330
That September he leave Georgia,

93
00:06:30,350 --> 00:06:32,020
skip his last year, and go pro.

94
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:34,890
Moves to South Carolina to train with Alleyne

95
00:06:34,910 --> 00:06:35,345
Francique.

96
00:06:35,365 --> 00:06:37,610
Sayin' he wanna be on the world stage.

97
00:06:38,665 --> 00:06:39,515
2024.

98
00:06:40,390 --> 00:06:41,540
The Olympic year.

99
00:06:49,630 --> 00:06:51,950
This the one everybody been waitin' on since

100
00:06:51,970 --> 00:06:54,030
that video in 2019.

101
00:06:54,530 --> 00:06:57,770
He run 44.84 in the 400.

102
00:06:57,790 --> 00:06:58,840
That's a PR.

103
00:06:59,510 --> 00:07:01,863
He get a World Indoor silver on the relay,

104
00:07:01,883 --> 00:07:03,960
and a World Relays gold.

105
00:07:04,330 --> 00:07:05,300
Then the Trials.

106
00:07:05,770 --> 00:07:09,747
In the 400, he make the final… and finish

107
00:07:09,783 --> 00:07:10,633
8th.

108
00:07:10,750 --> 00:07:11,450
Last.

109
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:13,413
In the 200?

110
00:07:13,523 --> 00:07:14,760
9th again.

111
00:07:15,190 --> 00:07:16,040
No final.

112
00:07:16,410 --> 00:07:18,220
And they don't pick him for the relay.

113
00:07:18,850 --> 00:07:24,867
No Paris.

114
00:07:29,877 --> 00:07:36,870
2025, he show up at Grand Slam Track in

115
00:07:36,890 --> 00:07:37,640
Philly.

116
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:40,680
7th in the 200, 20.87.

117
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:43,220
5th in the 400.

118
00:07:43,343 --> 00:07:47,900
This year he ran 45.51 in the 400.

119
00:07:48,090 --> 00:07:53,010
The kid that ran 9.98 at 18, his best 100

120
00:07:53,030 --> 00:07:56,345
today is still 9.98.

121
00:07:56,660 --> 00:07:59,040
Now I'ma keep it real with y'all.

122
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:01,840
Matthew Boling a 2-time world champion.

123
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:05,260
He ran sub-10 and sub-20.

124
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:08,440
Most people who ever put on spikes would

125
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:09,480
kill for that career.

126
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:12,250
But that ain't what we was promised.

127
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:14,720
We was promised the next Usain Bolt.

128
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:26,520
And that's the problem.

129
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:29,900
He went viral at 18 off a time that wasn't

130
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:30,460
even legal.

131
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:32,800
Before he ever ran a college race,

132
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:35,120
the whole internet already decided what

133
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:36,490
he was supposed to be.

134
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:39,180
And everything after that got measured against

135
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:42,330
1 clip with a 4.2 tailwind.

136
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:44,090
And the US?

137
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:47,270
It's the hardest team in the world to make.

138
00:08:47,310 --> 00:08:50,350
6th in America can be top 10 in the world.

139
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:53,170
But it still mean you stayin' home.

140
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:09,670
So was it a downfall?

141
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:13,550
Or was the hype just too big for anybody?

142
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:17,200
Let me know in the comments.

143
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:20,220
And if you was on the Boling hype train

144
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,760
in 2019… be honest.
